<!-- ============ HOW IT WORKS (flow) ============ -->
<section class="ac-royal sunk section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-header">
      <div class="section-eyebrow">How It Works</div>
      <h2 class="section-title">From new hire to certified.</h2>
      <p class="section-sub">Turnover means this path runs continuously rather than once at launch, so every stage is tracked and readiness is something you can report on.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="pathx" role="img" aria-label="A four stage path: the role assigns the learning path, the live catalog feeds the content, the associate practises with AI role-play, and certification is tracked by product and category.">
      <div class="pathx-rail"></div>
      <div class="pathx-step">
        <span class="pathx-dot"><i class="ti ti-user-check"></i></span>
        <strong>Role assigned</strong>
        <p>The learning path follows the role, so nobody is missed and nobody sits through the wrong module.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pathx-step">
        <span class="pathx-dot"><i class="ti ti-refresh"></i></span>
        <strong>Catalog syncs in</strong>
        <p>Training is built on live product data, so course content changes when the assortment does.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pathx-step">
        <span class="pathx-dot"><i class="ti ti-microphone"></i></span>
        <strong>Practice with AI role-play</strong>
        <p>Voice or text, scored on product knowledge, before the associate practises on a real customer.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pathx-step is-done">
        <span class="pathx-dot"><i class="ti ti-rosette-discount-check"></i></span>
        <strong>Certified to sell</strong>
        <p>Progress tracked by product and category, so readiness by store is a number rather than an impression.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

